{#- =========================================================================
    The workshop presentations' player (src/assets/js/presentations.js + presentations-core.js) — what the page
    needs for it, printed once where the page calls it (src/pages/orientation.njk):
      {% import "macros/presentations.njk" as pres with context %}{{ pres.player(lang) }}
    Context: `presentations` (src/_data/presentations.js: the decks' list) and the `url` filter (the path prefix).

    pres.player(lang) prints, all inert until the script uses them:
      #gvp-tpl      the dialog shell, cloned when a presentation is opened: progress line, the stage, the notes
                    panel, the presenter view's timer / clock / next slide, the Customize drawer (seven tabs; their
                    panels are drawn by the script), the overview, the control bar and its two menus (Print · More),
                    a live region and the toast. Every label in the page language; the slides inside are English
                    (marked lang="en" by the script; "(en inglés)" on /es/). Areas/presentations.css (prefix gvp-).
      #gvp-icons    the Lucide icons the script puts on the buttons it makes (Move up, Edit, Print …)
      #gvp-config   JSON for the script: the page language, the site's base path and the decks' JSON folder (both
                    with the path prefix), the decks (id, titles, slide count, versions — for the status lines,
                    without fetching anything) and every pres.* string (src/_i18n/presentations.json) in the page
                    language. "<" is written <, so no text can end the script element.
    The hooks on the cards (data-pres-open, data-pres-print, data-pres-status, data-pres-reset) are the page's own
    markup; presentations.js lists them. Without JavaScript none of this shows. -#}
{% macro player(lang) %}
{%- set decks = (presentations.decks if presentations and presentations.decks else []) -%}
{#- every string the script asks for (T("pres.…") / tInto(…, "pres.…") in presentations.js and the core's error
    keys); the markup below also builds some names from parts: pres.tab_version … pres.tab_edit … pres.tab_save,
    pres.print_slides / pres.print_slides_d, pres.print_notes_d, pres.print_handout_d, pres.print_script_d. The
    controls' names that {ui:…} in the notes asks for (customize_btn, the tabs …) are here too. -#}
